---
id: org.dxos.plugin.canvas
name: CanvasPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

An infinite, zoomable canvas of typed nodes and links at multiple depths, contributed to the illustrator
plugin as a drawing variant (`dxos.org/scene/1`). A drawing is a scene graph stored in ECHO as one record
per scene, node and link; a frame holds a child scene that opens in place and can show its contents live.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                        |
|--------|----------------------------|
| `test` | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`    |

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and an expectation (`expect`). Report
failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Draw, connect, and nest a scene on a canvas
  desc: The demo path — create a canvas drawing, draw and label shapes, connect them, and drill into a frame.
  actors: human
  covers: []
  status: passing            # 2026-10-09, recorded by autocue/draw-and-nest.mjs
  given:
    - an identity exists, on a fresh profile
    - plugin: Canvas is enabled in the plugin registry (it is off by default)
    - space: the default space is open on its Home
  steps:
    - name: Create a canvas drawing
      do: Click "Add to space", choose Drawing, pick the Canvas variant and click Create.
      expect: an empty canvas opens in a new plank, with the palette on its left
    - name: Draw and label shapes
      do: |
        With the Rectangle and Ellipse tools draw "Browser", "Agent" and "Space", double-clicking each to
        type its label; then draw a Frame and name it "Storage" in the Properties panel's Label field.
      expect: four labelled nodes on the canvas, and About counts 4 nodes
      note: A double-click on a frame opens its scene rather than editing its label.
    - name: Connect the shapes
      do: With the Smart line tool drag Browser→Space, Agent→Space and Space→Storage; then move Agent.
      expect: three links that follow the shapes as they move
    - name: Open the frame and draw inside it
      do: Click the frame's open control, draw and label "Objects" and "Sync", and link them.
      expect: the canvas drills into the frame's scene and the Up control is enabled
      note: The breadcrumb names the child scene "Untitled", not the frame's label.
    - name: Zoom back out and show the frame's contents
      do: Click Up, select the Storage frame, and turn on "Show contents" in the Properties panel.
      expect: the frame draws its nested scene live inside it

test QA-2: Draw a nested architecture diagram of composer-app
  desc: |
    A complex diagram across three scenes — composer-app's top level, with the plugins and the client each
    drawn as a nested scene inside a frame — every node and link taken from the packages' dependencies.
  actors: human
  covers: []
  status: passing            # 2026-10-09, recorded by autocue/composer-uml.mjs
  given:
    - an identity exists, on a fresh profile
    - plugin: Canvas is enabled in the plugin registry (it is off by default)
    - space: the default space is open on its Home
  steps:
    - name: Create a canvas drawing
      do: Click "Add to space", choose Drawing, pick the Canvas variant and click Create.
      expect: an empty canvas opens in a new plank, with the palette on its left
    - name: Draw the top level
      do: |
        Draw and label "Composer App" and "App Framework" (rectangles) and "EDGE" (ellipse); add two frames
        from the toolbar's "+" menu, name them "Plugins" and "Client" in the Properties panel's Label field,
        and move and resize each into place.
      expect: three labelled shapes and two labelled frames; About counts 5 nodes and 3 scenes
      note: |
        Frames come from the "+" menu, not the Frame tool: a frame drawn with the tool keeps the drag
        preview's child scene id, so every drawn frame shares one child scene (About stays at 2 scenes and
        each frame shows the other's contents).
    - name: Connect the top level by dependency
      do: |
        With the Smart line tool drag Composer App→Plugins, Composer App→App Framework,
        Plugins→App Framework, Plugins→Client and Client→EDGE.
      expect: five links, each attached to both of its ends
    - name: Open Plugins and draw the plugins inside it
      do: |
        Click the Plugins frame's open control; draw and label Sheet, Markdown, Table, Canvas, Illustrator
        and Space; link Sheet→Markdown, Markdown→Space, Table→Space, Canvas→Illustrator and Illustrator→Space.
      expect: the canvas drills into the frame's scene (Up enabled) and shows six nodes and five links
    - name: Open Client and draw its subsystems
      do: |
        Click Up, open the Client frame, draw and label Services, ECHO, HALO and MESH; link Services→ECHO,
        Services→HALO, Services→MESH and ECHO→MESH.
      expect: a second, separate nested scene with four nodes and four links
    - name: Go up and show both nested scenes live
      do: Click Up, then select each frame and turn on "Show contents" in the Properties panel.
      expect: each frame draws its own nested scene live inside it, alongside the top-level diagram
```
